# Adapt `tasks.md` to the igris plan format

`igris check` rejects the plan `tasks.md`. Your job: write a converted copy of it to

```
.igris/adapt/tasks.proposed.md
```

in the canonical igris format (reference at the end of this message), preserving every task, ID, description, dependency, status and model. Don't edit `tasks.md` itself: the owner reviews your proposal as a diff and decides whether it replaces the original.

## Model ranks

The Model column must hold one of these ranks from the project's `[models]` config (rank → Claude model):

- `haiku` → haiku
- `opus` → claude-opus-5-5
- `sonnet` → sonnet
- `—` for tasks without a session (Owner `user`)

## What you may change

- Restructure headings and tables: one `##` heading per phase, one task table per phase.
- Rename columns to the canonical names (ID, Task, Deps, Status, Model, Owner, Mode); keep any other column as it is.
- Normalize statuses to `ready`, `blocked`, `in progress`, `done` or `skipped`.
- Convert prose dependencies ("after the parser", "needs 2 and 3") into task IDs or ID ranges.
- Keep non-task content (introductions, legends, notes) as plain sections without a task table.

## What you must not change

- Don't invent, guess or change models. Map a model only when the original names it unambiguously (e.g. "Claude Opus" → `opus`).
- Don't drop, merge, split or reorder tasks, and don't add new ones.
- Don't rewrite descriptions: the Task cell keeps the original wording (escaping a `|` as `\|` is fine).
- Don't change task IDs. If a task has no ID or a duplicate one, ask the owner.

## Missing or unknown models

Give every agent task whose model is missing or doesn't map to a rank above Model `?`. `igris check` rejects `?`, so the owner fills these in after accepting. List each of them in a final section at the very end of the proposal:

```markdown
## Adapt notes

- M1-03: no model in the original
- M2-01: unknown model "gpt-4"
```

Use the same section for anything else the owner should check (columns you guessed, prose dependencies you interpreted). Leave it out when there's nothing to note.

## Finish

Ask the owner in this chat when anything is unclear and wait for the answer. Before finishing, check the proposal with

```
igris check --plan .igris/adapt/tasks.proposed.md
```

and fix every problem it reports except the `?` models. When `.igris/adapt/tasks.proposed.md` is complete, run this as your very last action:

```
igris done ADAPT --note "<one-line summary of the conversion>"
```

